[{"q":"The police emergency number often taught is ____.","options":["12","199","7777","0000"],"answer":1,"explain":"199 can reach the police."},{"q":"Do not fight. Fighting can cause ____.","options":["better exam scores","more friends always","injury","peace always"],"answer":2,"explain":"Use words or a teacher, not fists."},{"q":"A whistle can be used to ____ for help.","options":["iron","call","cook","sweep"],"answer":1,"explain":"Loud signals attract attention."},{"q":"Security education teaches us to stay ____.","options":["away from school","afraid of everyone forever","safe","silent in class always"],"answer":2,"explain":"Be alert, not fearful."},{"q":"Nigeria’s national emergency number is ____.","options":["112","000","911 only as the only option","1234"],"answer":0,"explain":"112 is the national emergency number."},{"q":"If a stranger asks you to go with them, you should ____.","options":["follow quietly","keep it secret","say no and tell an adult","enter the car"],"answer":2,"explain":"Never go with a stranger."},{"q":"Cyber predators may pretend to be ____.","options":["your head teacher in person","the school bell","children or friends","your parent at home"],"answer":2,"explain":"Never meet an online stranger alone."},{"q":"The assembly point is where we ____ in an emergency.","options":["hide from teachers","play football first","meet","buy snacks"],"answer":2,"explain":"Schools have assembly points."},{"q":"Your body is private. If someone touches you in a bad way, ____.","options":["tell a trusted adult","keep silent forever","blame yourself","hide at the market"],"answer":0,"explain":"It is not your fault. Speak up."},{"q":"Do not take gifts from ____.","options":["strangers","your teacher as a prize","your parents","grandparents"],"answer":0,"explain":"Strangers may not be safe."},{"q":"Medicines at home should be kept ____.","options":["out of children’s reach","on the floor","in drink bottles","next to sweets"],"answer":0,"explain":"Wrong medicine is dangerous."},{"q":"Flood safety: do not walk in ____ water.","options":["a puddle with an adult on the compound","a shallow known gutter at home never anyway wait","fast or deep","a bath"],"answer":2,"explain":"Flood water can hide holes and germs."},{"q":"Online, do not share your ____.","options":["favourite subject","first name only with teacher","class","address and password"],"answer":3,"explain":"Personal data can be misused."},{"q":"Do not walk alone in ____ places.","options":["your living room","dark lonely","a busy school corridor","a supervised playground"],"answer":1,"explain":"Stay where people can see you."},{"q":"A strong password should not be ____.","options":["a mix of letters and numbers","long","1234 or your name","secret"],"answer":2,"explain":"Guessable passwords are weak."},{"q":"Do not take ____ given by friends without an adult’s knowledge.","options":["your own water bottle","your own lunch","a textbook","unknown drugs or tablets"],"answer":3,"explain":"Unknown substances can harm you."},{"q":"Wear a ____ in a car.","options":["seat belt","blindfold","loose scarf on the door","school bag on the head"],"answer":0,"explain":"Seat belts save lives."},{"q":"Bullying should be ____.","options":["copied","praised","reported","kept as a secret always"],"answer":2,"explain":"Tell a teacher."},{"q":"School ID and visitors’ passes help to ____.","options":["decorate only","cook","know who belongs","play football"],"answer":2,"explain":"Visitors should report at the gate."},{"q":"When cycling, wear a ____.","options":["earphones at full volume always","blindfold","helmet","long loose scarf in the wheel"],"answer":2,"explain":"Helmets protect the head."},{"q":"Do not put ____ in sockets.","options":["a charger the right way","nothing always including plugs","fingers or metal","the plug of a safe appliance"],"answer":2,"explain":"Electric shock is dangerous."},{"q":"In a fire, ____ to the nearest exit.","options":["use the lift in a burning house if told never","move quickly and calmly","hide under a nylon bag","go back for toys first always"],"answer":1,"explain":"Know the escape route. Don’t use lifts in a fire."},{"q":"When the alarm rings, ____.","options":["ignore it","lock yourself in the toilet always","run in any direction screaming only","follow emergency instructions"],"answer":3,"explain":"Practise drills seriously."},{"q":"If you get lost in a market, ____.","options":["leave town","stay put and look for a security post / tell a seller with a stall to find police","hide in a boot of a car","follow any stranger home"],"answer":1,"explain":"Stay visible and ask official help."},{"q":"Do not play with ____.","options":["story books","a football in a field","puzzles","fire and matches"],"answer":3,"explain":"Fire can burn."},{"q":"In a stampede, move ____ the crowd if you can, protect your chest.","options":["by sitting in the middle","deeper into","sideways out of","against blindly"],"answer":2,"explain":"Protect yourself; don’t push."},{"q":"A good security habit at home is to ____ the door.","options":["tell strangers where the key is","lock","leave wide open at night always","hide the key under the mat always"],"answer":1,"explain":"Lock doors and windows."},{"q":"If you are in danger, tell a ____ adult.","options":["a stray animal","unknown online only","trusted","nobody"],"answer":2,"explain":"Parents, teachers and police can help."},{"q":"Report suspicious bags in public to ____.","options":["a stranger to open it","nobody","your younger sibling only","security / police"],"answer":3,"explain":"Do not touch unknown packages."},{"q":"When crossing the road, look ____, right and left again.","options":["at the sky only","at your phone only","backwards only","left"],"answer":3,"explain":"Stop, look and listen."},{"q":"Which is a safe action?","options":["telling a teacher about bullying","swimming in a flood","keeping abuse secret","playing with matches"],"answer":0,"explain":"That action helps k